      "message": "In `zephyr/test/fingerprint/task/include/fpsensor_test_utils.h`, the header guard is defined as:\n\n```cpp\n#ifndef __TASK_FPSENSOR_TEST_UTILS_H\n#define __TASK_FPSENSOR_TEST_UTILS_H\n\n```\n\nIn C++, identifiers that begin with two consecutive underscores (or an underscore followed by a capital letter) are strictly reserved for the compiler and standard library implementation. Using them can technically lead to undefined behavior or conflicts.\n\n**Suggestion:** Remove the leading underscores. A standard, safe format would be:\n\n```cpp\n#ifndef TASK_FPSENSOR_TEST_UTILS_H_\n#define TASK_FPSENSOR_TEST_UTILS_H_\n\n```",
